egion or piece that it holds as material and does not plan (under Min Region Cut Length, no Geodesic Adaptive field). When one still holds stock at the end of the plan, the op raises `geom.rough_left_stock` (Caution, a warning): the counts, the area, the tallest stock and its position, and whether the op publishes its rest regions for a toolpath boundary. The export names it in the G-code header and in `summary.json` (`Gate::RoughLeftStock`). Sentry: `--lib _p37`. P44 (2026-11-21): the small-area bound is removed (BREAK: a rough plans the small regions that it dropped before; the one drop rule of a region is Min Region Cut Length, read as the length of the contour line of the region). On remaining stock a region with no room for the Geodesic Adaptive field (a slot a little wider than the tool) is cut along its contour line, one Depth/Pass per level; on a fresh block such a region stays and the finding names it. The finding lists each place where the tool fits, stock stands and a drop record says why (position, area, height, reason; the 12 largest); the places with no drop record are one count and one area and do not raise the finding alone. No pass cuts a strip that makes no region at a wall. Sentry: `--lib _p44` |
